FORKING : Copy repo from 3rd person repository to our own called forking and then do the changes locally.

git clone #clone from github to git in the local
git pull  or git pull --force # last changes to local repo
git remote   # git remote destination details
git push --force push latest changes to remote repo
git reset --hard  #git memory clean rarely used or tidy up your code before commit
git revert <commit id>  # revert the changes
git checkout <brnch name >  #switch between branches
git branch #create new branch
git merge #combined the specific branch with main branch
git branch -d   # delete branch
git stash #temporary save of the code locally
git rebase  ##which allows for applying changes from one branch onto another
